      "provider": "provider[\"registry.opentofu.org/integrations/github\"]",
      "instances": [
        {
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "description": "The BuildBuddy GitHub app unlocks new features for your Bazel builds, such as:\r\n\r\n* **GitHub statuses for Bazel builds**: Get a GitHub status reported for your commit indicating whether your Bazel build passed or succeeded. The status contains a link to BuildBuddy's build results UI which lets you dive deep into your build. (Note: this requires configuring build metadata including `ROLE=CI`; see our [metadata guide](https://www.buildbuddy.io/docs/guide-metadata) for more info)\r\n* **BuildBuddy Workflows**: Build and test your Bazel repository at every commit, with BuildBuddy's hosted, warm Bazel instances. [Learn more about BuildBuddy workflows](https://www.buildbuddy.io/docs/workflows-introduction)\r\n\r\n## Repo authorization\r\n\r\nYou can choose to install BuildBuddy for all repos, or install it only for particular repos. Once you've installed the app, you'll be redirected to BuildBuddy to link the app installation to your BuildBuddy organization. You can use the \"Workflows\" page to enable workflows for individual repositories.",
            "id": "317600",
            "name": "buildbuddy.io",
            "node_id": "A_kwHOA4rW0M4ABNig",
